{"_readme":"FIXTURE for ui-audit --selfcheck. Synthetic --uiaudit draw records, NOT captured from a cart. Screen is 320x200. Entry kinds: t=text (t=the string, c=1 means inside a clip() scissor), f=fill, w=ui.h widget. Draw order = array order, which is what the occlusion rule reads. Frames 0-5 carry the STEADY findings (>= the default 3-frame persistence); frame 2 additionally carries one 1-frame TRANSIENT. The ZOOM/ALPHA pair is drawn in REVERSE alphabetical order on purpose: its waiver must match by sorted identity, and an order-sensitive comparison would still pass on the AAA/BBB pair (which is already alphabetical). See README.md for the full table. This line is ignored: the loader skips any record with no f/sw/sh."}
